Given, $V_{1}=V, l_{1}=l, r_{1}=r \begin{aligned}$&l_{2}=2 l_{1}=2 l \\
&r_{2}=$\frac{r_{1}}{2}=\frac{r}{2}$\\
&V_{2}=?
\end{aligned}

According$ to Poiseuille's formula, the rate of flow of liquid through a narrow tube is given as\begin{aligned}$& V=$\frac{\pi p r^{4}}{8 n l}$\\
\Rightarrow \quad & V \propto $\frac{r^{4}}{l}$\\
\Rightarrow \quad & $\frac{V_{2}}{V_{1}}=\left(\frac{r_{2}}{r_{1}}\right)^{4} \cdot \frac{l_{1}}{l_{2}}
\end{aligned}

\begin{aligned}$&=$\left(\frac{r / 2}{r}\right)^{4}\left(\frac{l}{2 l}\right)=\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{4} \cdot \frac{1}{2}=\frac{1}{32}$\\
\Rightarrow \quad \quad V_{2} &=$\frac{V_{1}}{32}=\frac{V}{32}
\end{aligned}$
